WEBVTT

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:42.650
In ancient times, when the ancestor of the Queen descended from Ephon Noha to Tahai Aze,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.870
the people met the Founding King, Je, who was tall and had golden eyes.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:51.620
It was the holy God Himself.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.810
So many thousands of days and nights later,

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.770
since the capital governed by the Queen does not have an army,

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.110
it is now currently protected by the Grand Duke,

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:09.070
who possesses an army specializing in Touda, and technically governs the quarters on the other side of the mountains.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:18.370
Erin, who was raised in a village with Touda, started her new life with Jone the honey man.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:29.920
Right as Spring was coming to an end, Jone told Erin that they were moving to a summer cabin on Mt. Kasho.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.590
Today's the day of the move.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:12.760
The party is hiking up the mountain toward the cabin.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:21.290
How much farther are they taking us?

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.560
It's so beautiful!

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:42.620
When the flowers reach full bloom, this entire place becomes covered in white, just like snow.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.620
See that pointy roof there?

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.270
That's the summer cabin.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.440
I'm going on ahead!

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:01.010
Hey!  It's dangerous to run around here!

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.850
See what I said?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:28.080
The Platinum White Feather

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:33.610
Capital The Palace

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:47.180
Seimiya

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.450
My dear Seimiya, how are you today?
Seimiya

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.950
My dear Seimiya, how are you today?

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.270
Oji-sama!

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.690
When did you return?

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.610
Damiya

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.780
I returned only a moment ago.
Damiya

00:04:58.780 --> 00:04:58.800
Damiya

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.320
I started to miss the sweet and sour scent of these flowers.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.870
This garden is magnificent, no matter when I see it.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.250
After all, I'm taking care of each flower with love.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.550
Seimiya, you're lovelier than any flower that blooms here.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.800
Oh please, Oji-sama.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.480
Welcome back, Damiya.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:38.550
You look well.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.030
Queen
You look well.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.470
Queen

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.910
I'm glad to see you're doing well too, dear Aunt.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.740
How was the Grand Duke doing?

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.160
Well, as always.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:56.860
His two sons have grown big and strong, too.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.170
Shunan and Ngan, am I right?

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:04.410
That's great to hear.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.720
Then here's one more story to tell.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.930
Wild beast-lords have started building their nests at Mt. Kasho.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.060
The beast-lords have?

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.690
That is wonderful.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:21.440
I have already sent a warden to Mt. Kasho to investigate.

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:26.760
I'm sure he'll return with good news.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.420
I'll open it right away, so hold on a second.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.720
It's open!

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:05.860
Coming!

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:11.160
Please enter, Lady Erin.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.190
A fireplace?

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:32.260
This area gets cold, even during summer.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.920
We can't keep ourselves comfortable without a fire.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.480
Really?

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.770
Whoa there.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.250
Looks like the floor has rotted.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.540
I guess we have a lot of repairing to do around here.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.490
Oji-san, what's this?

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:54.950
Ah, that's my loincloth.  I forgot it here last year.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.080
It's already washed, so don't worry.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.920
But now it's covered in dust, so I can't use it as is.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:09.420
After all, there's a year's worth of dust in this place right now.

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.640
We have some major cleaning up to do.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:46.420
Looks nice.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.770
What is in those boxes?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.060
There we go.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.000
Next one up.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.310
Wow, it's a centipede!

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:44.590
What?

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:47.500
Ah!

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:55.020
What's wrong, little girl?

00:09:58.550 --> 00:09:59.870
Look at your face!

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:26.480
Hey, are we not done yet?!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.610
Not yet!

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:33.280
I'm almost done, so hang in there.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.990
I-I'm sorry.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.450
It's fine.  Don't worry about it.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:42.540
You shouldn't be laughing!

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:56.610
I thought something flew by just now...

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:59.100
What's wrong?!

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:04.500
That's strange.  I'm sure something flew by, but...

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.200
What's that?

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.410
Oji-san!  I'm going into the forest for a bit!

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.590
Okay...

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.960
Wait, little girl!

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.320
A shining tree?

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.450
Yup!  In the forest.

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.600
You sure you weren't seeing stuff?

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:48.190
Yes.  I'm sure something was shining around here.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:52.900
I can't imagine a large gold nugget falling from the sky.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.850
D-Don't stop so suddenly.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.480
What is this?

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.950
Could it be a footprint?

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:17.070
No way.  A footprint this big isn't possible.

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:19.680
If something like that existed...

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:28.640
Monster human!

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.520
R-Run!

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:51.830
It must've been this.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:11.190
Oji-san!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.970
Oji-san, Oji-san!  Look!

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:28.910
That's a beast-lord's feather.

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:32.190
Who are you?

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:34.830
Kalon!  Is that you, Kalon?

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:37.300
Long time no see!

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:39.800
Welcome!

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:43.680
I had business around here, so I stopped by.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:47.060
Sorry, I let myself in to wait.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:52.130
No big deal.  I was out picking some firewood.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:53.900
Oh yeah.  This is Erin.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:56.020
We're living together right now due to certain circumstances.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.520
Nice to meet you, Erin-chan.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:04.820
There's nothing to worry about.  He's Kalon, my old...

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:12.040
Ah...  My old friend.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:17.260
All my buddies from Tamuiwan wanted to see you, too.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:19.530
I see.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:31.970
But Kalon, I'm surprised you knew that I was at this cabin.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:36.440
You once sent me a letter from here.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.440
Is everyone doing well?

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:46.160
Yes.  Some have become wardens, like me, and others have become government officials or reverends.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:50.120
They're all walking their own paths.

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.420
I see.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:01.550
So you came to Mt. Kasho for the Queen?

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:05.010
Yes, we heard that a beast-lord is on this mountain.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:07.050
"Beast-lord?"

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:10.050
You don't know of the beast-lords?

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.080
No.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:16.770
Beast-lords are creatures that have been worshiped as sacred animals in this country for a long time.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:21.230
The feather you picked up in the forest must have belonged to a wild beast-lord.

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:23.860
That's a beast-lord's feather?

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:32.740
They've got the face of a wolf, and have a large pair of wings and sharp claws.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:38.710
As the name implies, they lord over all the beasts in this world.

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:41.930
Are beast-lords bigger than Touda?

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:43.240
Of course.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:47.260
Fully grown beast-lords are far larger than Touda.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:54.430
I never knew there were beasts bigger than those Touda.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:06.900
It's said that misery will befall this country if the number of beast-lords diminish.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:13.870
That's why wardens, like me, along with beast-lord rangers, look for the wild beast-lords' nests

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:18.080
and capture the babies to take them to a care center to make sure the count remains high.

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:34.220
At the capital, under the law for beast-lord regulation, many babies are being taken care of with great diligence.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.950
Capture the babies and raise them...

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:43.770
Erin was remembering Ake Village.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:51.550
Because, in Ake Village, they hunt for eggs once a year to make sure the Touda count doesn't diminish.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:04.020
All right then, let's have a concert tonight.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.410
This reminds me of the old days.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:11.930
Those days when we were on the hill in Wazal.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.000
Those were fun days.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:42.410
You're both so good!

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:05.060
That was so nice.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:07.590
How's that?  Pretty good, eh?

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:11.320
Not only can I play, but I can even make one.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.300
Really?

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.550
You can play a harp?

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.510
No.  This is my first time.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.120
First time?!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:45.990
I only heard that tune just now, and it sounded nice, so I tried mimicking it.

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:56.740
This is unbelievable.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.300
Did you really hear the tune for the first time?

00:18:59.300 --> 00:18:59.950
Yes.

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:05.240
She's got an amazing sense of pitch to memorize a tune after just hearing it once.

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:06.960
I'm surprised, too.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:49.950
All right, it's my turn next.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.360
I'll play a song I created.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:07.350
